1
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:01,000
Meet Rainbow Dash and Rarity the Unicorn!

2
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:56,000
My Little Pony: The Runaway Rainbow is a animation,
adventure, fantasy film directed by Victor Dal Chele.

3
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:51,000
Rainbow Dash loves the time of year when Ponyville and Breezie
Blossom are all about celebrating rainbows.

4
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:46,000
Meanwhile in a new magical place called Unicornia, Rarity is being taught how to be a
Unicorn Princess and the importance of making the first rainbow of the season.

5
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:41,000
But she is quite a little rascal and embarks on an incredible ride, a huge
adventure (with lots of mishaps) as she tries to get back to Unicornia.

6
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:36,000
Rarity soon realizes that getting home in time to create the first rainbow
of season is not an easy thing to do --- but it is fun!

7
00:13:25,000 --> 00:13:31,000
Sweetberry (voice), played by Kathleen Barr.

8
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:26,000
Brights Brightly (voice), played by Maryke Hendrikse.

9
00:17:15,000 --> 00:17:21,000
Pinkie Pie (voice), played by Janyse Jaud.

10
00:19:10,000 --> 00:19:16,000
Sunny Daze / Coconut Cream (voice), played by Adrienne Carter.

11
00:21:05,000 --> 00:21:11,000
Spike (voice), played by Brian Drummond.

12
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:06,000
Zipzee (voice), played by Andrea Libman.

13
00:24:55,000 --> 00:25:01,000
My Little Pony Crystal Princess: The Runaway Rainbow is a 2006 direct-to-video animated musical fantasy adventure film 
produced by SD Entertainment and distributed by Paramount Home Entertainment in association with Hasbro.

14
00:26:50,000 --> 00:26:56,000
The film is the third feature in the third incarnation of the My Little Pony
series and the second film to promote the Crystal Princess line.

15
00:28:45,000 --> 00:28:51,000
Unlike The Princess Promenade, the film has been criticized.

16
00:30:40,000 --> 00:30:46,000
The DVD also features two more animated features, Greetings from Unicornia and Friends
are Never Far Away, which was originally released on video in 2005.

17
00:32:35,000 --> 00:32:41,000
The Runaway Rainbow was made available on hubworld.com (a successor of Hasbro's MonkeyBarTV website),
alongside My Little Pony: A Very Minty Christmas and My Little Pony: The Princess Promenade.

18
00:34:30,000 --> 00:34:36,000
But they were removed from the site later.

19
00:36:25,000 --> 00:36:31,000
The movie has been reissued in the 2-disc DVD collection My Little Pony: Classic Movie Collection,
alongside The Princess Promenade, Dancing in the Clouds and Friends are Never Far Away.

20
00:38:20,000 --> 00:38:26,000
Alongside The Princess Promenade and Twinkle Wish Adventure, the film premiered on August
8, 2014 on the Hub Network after its "My Little Pony Mega Mare-athon".

21
00:40:15,000 --> 00:40:21,000
According to Broadway World, the "Mega Mare-athon" itself drew in 5.4 million viewers and has earned significant delivery growth on every demographic: Kids 2-11 (+134%), Girls 2-11
(+179%), Kids 6-11 (+169%), Girls 6-11 (+216%), Adults 18-49 (+111%), Women 18-49 (+146%), Adults 25-54 (+74%), Women 25-54 (+76%), Persons 2+ (+124%) and Households (+98%).

22
00:42:10,000 --> 00:42:16,000
The film explores themes of anthropomorphism, based on toy, unicorn.

23
00:44:05,000 --> 00:44:11,000
The tone is lighthearted.
